parameters.text:
=You write social media copy for one product from a small online shop. Use ONLY the facts below.

Product title: {{ $json.title }}
Shop: {{ $json.shop_name }}
Product type: {{ $json.product_type || 'not stated' }}
Tags: {{ ($json.tags || []).join(', ') || 'none' }}
Materials: {{ ($json.materials || []).join(', ') || 'not stated' }}
Listing description:
"""
{{ $json.description_text || 'none' }}
"""

Write in {{ $('Configure Catalog Settings').first().json.caption_language }}. Tone: {{ $('Configure Catalog Settings').first().json.caption_tone }}

Rules:
- Only use facts stated above. If a detail is not stated, leave it out. Never guess sizes, colors, materials or uses.
- Never mention prices, discounts, sales, coupons, stock levels, shipping times or delivery promises, even if the description does. Prices are added separately.
- Never write reviews, ratings, stars, testimonials, customer quotes, bestseller status, awards or numbers that are not in the listing.
- No health, safety, eco or certification claims unless the description states them.
- short_name: the plain product name, at most 60 characters, no keyword lists.
- pinterest_title: at most 100 characters, clear and searchable, starts with the main product keyword.
- pinterest_description: 2 or 3 sentences, at most 450 characters, with natural keywords a buyer would search for on Pinterest. No hashtags, no links.
- instagram_caption: 2 to 4 short sentences, then 3 to 5 relevant hashtags. No links.
- facebook_caption: 1 to 3 sentences, no hashtags, no links (the product link is added automatically).
- threads_caption: 1 or 2 sentences, at most 300 characters, no links.

